`/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-15_B1567_STATUS.md`. First line `B1567 STATUS (placeholder, Step 0 running)`. Sections: Questions, BLUF, Step 0, Step 1, PRIOR WORK, COMMIT A, the chain log (clock, runs, tallies, load1 per step), MUTATIONS, `## READY`, ADDENDA READ, NOT TESTED, Corrections. **The LAST line on finish is exactly one of:** `READY B1567: <head sha40>`, `HANDOVER B1567: next <part> <step> | done <parts>`, or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`. In between: `WORKING: ...`. Poll `ls /Volumes/Datasec_DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/tuesday/briefs/ | /usr/bin/grep -i -E '^2026-11-1[5-9]_B1567_(ADDENDUM|ANSWER)'` at every step boundary (control: the same grep with `SEAT-N129` lists this kit); a new file is read whole, binds you, and is named in ADDENDA READ before you act on it.

## STANDING LINES
PRIOR-WORK CHECK (a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). No deploy, no PR, no merge to main, no Jira, no mail, no message to any human. Never delete (quarantine). Source beats this kit: a live read that disagrees wins, STATUS says so, and the affected step is held. Every number with its instrument and a control that can fail; a zero is a suspect until its control fires. No product file edited; no new customer-visible word anywhere.


